THE SAME wkv7 SOURCES APPEAR TWICE IN THE ARCHIVE and are identical: `diff` of
RWKV-v5/cuda/wkv7_cuda.cu against RWKV-v7/train_temp/cuda/wkv7_cuda.cu is empty.
RWKV-v5/ was taken because RWKV-v5/src/model.py is the file that also holds the
RWKV-7 time mixing this kernel serves (RWKV_Tmix_x070), so the kernel and its
caller come from one upstream file pair rather than two.

THIS IS THE "wind_backstepping" KERNEL: a chunked RWKV-7 WKV in bf16, CHUNK_LEN 16,
compiled with -D_C_=<head size> -D_CHUNK_LEN_=16.  RWKV-v7/train_temp/ additionally
ships ten more fused .cu files for an experimental training stack; none of them were
taken, because the benchmark swaps a MIXER into mira_llm's block and those kernels
fuse the surrounding channel mixing, the loss and the head as well.

HOW IT IS BUILT HERE.  Upstream compiles this pair at import time with
torch.utils.cpp_extension.load; kernel/cuda/rwkv_v7/upstream.py does the same, with
upstream's flags, against these files.
